<title>ESTONIA: NOON RADIO HEADLINES - JULY 2.</title>
<headline>NOON RADIO HEADLINES - JULY 2.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the main headlines from Estonia's Kuku radio news report on Wednesday at noon. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- President Meri approved nine laws including an energy act and the supplementary budget.</p>
<p>- Two women fell off a bridge over the Lasnamae highway near Tallinn.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
